WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:31.787 --> 00:00:33.460
Bwiti is a spiritual practice

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.780
that forest-dwelling tribes of West Africa

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.103
have been observing for untold millennia.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:47.850
At the center of this
practice is the iboga root,

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.850
a plant indigenous to West Africa

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.770
with powerful psychoactive effects,

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:53.263
which can last for days.

00:00:55.448 --> 00:00:57.480
Initiates are believed
to commune with the dead,

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.683
and it is believed to heal many ailments.

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:06.283
Many locals consider this ancient
practice witchcraft today,

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.010
but Westerners have
been increasingly drawn

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:12.730
to Bwiti and the mysterious iboga plant,

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.373
to cure a widespread modern affliction.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.410
The opioid crisis may be far worse

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:22.520
than initially thought.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.560
We've interviewed lawmakers
on the left and the right.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.433
They all say opioid
addiction is a problem.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.270
Many believe that this
ancient psychedelic root

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:33.970
is the key to curing addiction.

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:35.810
You know, there is no other compound

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:36.980
that will stop somebody

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:39.800
from physically withdrawing on opiates.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.283
It's the only one.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.080
Now, science is rigorously testing

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.730
this hypothesis.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:49.360
Biotech companies are creating
analogues of ibogaine,

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.180
the primary component of the plant,

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.150
and pushing for FDA approval

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.360
to help curb the disastrous effects

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.793
of the opioid epidemic.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.440
If successful, this mysterious compound

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.570
could have the power to heal millions,

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.140
while seriously disrupting

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.383
the multi-billion dollar opioid market.

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:19.810
In the US alone, over
81,000 drug overdose deaths

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:22.210
occur between 2019 and 2020.

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:23.520
As more data comes in,

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.380
that number is expected to be higher,

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.400
and the CDC estimates that overdoses

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:30.023
will exceed a hundred thousand in 2021.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.490
The situation couldn't be more urgent,

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.970
and addicts are increasingly
turning to iboga

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:39.130
after trying everything
else to kick their habits.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.020
Usually, they hear it from word of mouth,

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.310
and they have to travel abroad

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:45.183
since the substance remains
illegal in the United States.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:48.340
An underground cottage industry has formed

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:51.823
in all corners of the world
where iboga is not regulated.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:59.853
This is the place people
come when, you know,

00:02:59.853 --> 00:03:01.470
they've tried everything else.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.568
And fortunately, it's something

00:03:03.568 --> 00:03:06.400
that really, really works for them.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:09.340
Thank you, mother nature,
for creating iboga

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:12.920
and giving us a tool to go
deep inside of ourselves.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.800
Levi Barker has embraced
the Bwiti traditions

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.400
and now runs a shamanistic healing center

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.290
in Costa Rica called Iboga Wellness.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:22.760
A former addict himself,

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:25.203
he knows the power of
the plant first-hand.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:28.830
I was kind of the first generation

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:32.720
of the opioid epidemic that came through.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.950
I had a snowboarding
accident when I was 19,

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.150
got prescribed some Percocet, you know,

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:41.310
started taking them, started liking them,

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.700
kept growing from there
and went through, you know,

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.220
every opioid pill you can imagine.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:49.200
And eventually, that
led to heroin as well.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.843
And so a dear friend of
mine mentioned iboga.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.150
I was able to just lay there

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:02.080
and let it come in and cleanse me.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:07.080
And so, I woke up the next
day physically free of drugs.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.850
And so I knew from that point forward

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.480
that I wanted to work with it.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.450
So, Levi, tell me, what exactly do we know

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.180
about this plant and how it works?

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:17.210
With a lot of psychedelics,

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:19.690
nobody's exactly sure how it works,

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.770
but at least here, you
keep seeing people come in

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:25.833
and getting healed for a
wide variety of issues.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:27.960
You know it does work

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:31.373
because it changes lives
and people report back.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.530
Just as with the original Bwiti,

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:36.610
the detox process last days

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.620
and involves a carefully crafted setting

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:40.380
as patients ingest the plant.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.270
People come and get the treatment.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:43.450
They have some time afterwards

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:44.850
where they get the proper coaching

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.610
and then definitely,
some after-care involved.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:50.440
And, you know, it's just a long process

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:52.740
especially when you're
dealing with opiate addicts.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:57.740
I mean, that's at least a three
to six-day process for them.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:01.280
But sending every addict abroad

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.230
for a week-long journey
to kick their addiction

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:04.890
just isn't practical.

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:07.210
And if it's ever possible
to scale this to the level

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:09.300
we would need to make
a dent in the epidemic,

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:11.700
we're going to need the
help of modern medicine.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:15.280
My name is Andrew Kruegel.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.380
I am a medicinal chemist and entrepreneur.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.480
Okay, help me understand

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:22.947
the difference between iboga and ibogaine.

00:05:22.947 --> 00:05:26.600
Ibogaine is the major active constituent

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.980
of the Tabernanthe iboga plant.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.390
So, the plant itself contains

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:33.950
a number of different
psychoactive compounds,

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:36.750
and ibogaine as the most
well-known of those.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.040
That was first noted by a man

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:42.120
named Howard Lotsof in the 1960s,

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:45.310
who had had a long history
of addiction to heroin,

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.770
and he visited Western Africa

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:53.200
looking for potential ways
to treat his affliction.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.400
And he ended up going
through an iboga ceremony

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:57.640
with the native people there,

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:01.750
and found himself cured
of his heroin addiction.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.760
He brought that knowledge back to the West

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:04.973
and popularized it.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:07.880
But just as soon as it was popularized,

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.300
it was labeled dangerous
with no medical use.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.500
In order to fight and defeat this enemy,

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:17.210
it is necessary to wage
a new, all-out offensive.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:20.740
It got pulled in with all the
other psychoactive compounds

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:25.020
into the Schedule I
classification at that time,

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.530
despite the fact that
there's no real history

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:31.670
of abuse of ibogaine for
recreational purposes.

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:34.120
In fact, the ibogaine trip is not really

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.370
a recreational experience at all.

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:37.540
The drugs legal status

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:39.420
is only one of its hurdles.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:41.940
There are also some
serious safety concerns,

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:44.040
including its high toxicity levels

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.570
and a tendency to induce
cardiac arrhythmias,

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:49.723
which in rare circumstances,
have resulted in death.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:54.760
Ibogaine blocks a ion channel in the heart

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.360
called the hERG channel, and
blocking this ion channel

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:01.300
can cause what's called QT prolongation.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:04.160
So the part of the heart
rhythm gets elongated,

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:07.280
and that has led to some deaths

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.710
under the sort of
uncontrolled circumstances

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:11.290
in which it's used.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:13.250
We think that ibogaine itself

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.640
under a more controlled setting

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:17.420
with proper EKG monitoring,

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:19.660
could be safe enough already to use,

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.030
but with our novel analogues,

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:24.660
we're trying to reduce
inhibition of that hERG channel,

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:28.530
and thereby attenuate those cardiac risks.

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:29.450
But for many people

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:31.300
desperate to kick their addiction,

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.730
they're already willing to take that risk.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:35.530
In recent years, Levi's clinic has seen

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:37.210
a surge in clients looking for help

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:39.100
with more than just opioid addiction.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:42.850
We have people come here for over-eating.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:45.770
Some people have sex or porn addictions.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:48.560
People get addicted to
thinking in the past,

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.590
or they grew up with
different belief systems

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:52.873
that just filters their whole worldview.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:56.850
And this is really where science hits

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:59.360
a blind spot, since no
large clinical trials

00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:01.000
have taken place with ibogaine,

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.450
and anecdotes like Levi's
are not going to get far

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:06.130
when it comes to FDA approvals.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.040
There's certainly a large amount

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:10.770
of anecdotal data to support its efficacy,

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:14.150
and those small trials and anecdotes

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:17.120
support it being extremely efficacious,

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:20.680
not just in opioid addiction,
but also in alcoholism,

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:23.330
psychostimulant addiction, et cetera.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:26.020
But it's never been
tested in a serious trial

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:29.740
with hundreds of patients
and appropriate controls.

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:33.040
So, until that's done, we
can't say with any certainty

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.360
that this is actually going to work.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:38.000
So there's this study
published in December of 2020.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.220
It's a non-toxic ibogaine analogue

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:42.480
that separates the psychoactive effects

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.700
from the anti-addictive properties.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.720
It was successfully tested on rodents,

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:50.200
which is a long way from
being tested on humans.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:51.130
Now, do you think there's a need

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.540
for the psychoactive element

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:54.270
for this drug to properly work?

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:56.330
Or can we just extract these molecules,

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:58.010
separate them, and take what we need?

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:00.610
I think that's the big question to answer,

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:02.420
not just in ibogaine research,

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:05.611
but in psychedelic
research across the board.

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:13.070
Whether the higher level
cognitive experience

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:17.090
of a hallucinogenic
transformative experience

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:19.970
is what drives the
efficacy, or if it's simply

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:22.870
underlying neurobiological changes

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:25.950
that we're not really aware
of at the conscious level.

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:26.890
And I think it's possible

00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:28.890
that both things are important.

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:30.070
You might be aware of this

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:32.240
transformative psychedelic experience

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:35.320
while you're on the drug,
but behind the scenes,

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:38.680
there may also be a resetting
of your reward circuitry

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.950
and that sets on nerve root factors

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:45.460
in the nucleus accumbens or
the ventral tegmental area

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:48.180
that actually physically reset

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:50.580
some of the bad connectivity
that has developed

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:53.420
as the result of an addictive history.

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:55.640
But we don't really understand

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:59.430
the neurobiological underpinnings
of human consciousness.

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:01.400
Trying to unravel that mystery

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:04.660
is sort of also unraveling the mystery

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:06.803
of what makes us human, right?

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:12.450
That mystery is not
scaring away investors,

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:15.420
who not only firmly believe
in ibogaine's efficacy,

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.790
but aim to cut into the
profits that big pharma

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:20.423
has reaped for years
off of opioid addiction.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:23.820
The addiction industry in the US

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:25.990
is a $42 billion market.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:28.410
And that market is expected to grow

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:31.210
to about 54 billion by 2025.

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:34.430
The growing size of the
opioid use disorder market

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:38.100
is what's actually incited a
lot of the psychedelic biotechs

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:40.060
to address this gap in the market.

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:42.130
But the substance is very understudied

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:44.140
and it remains a Schedule I drug.

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:46.320
Doesn't that make it kind
of a risky bet for you?

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:49.330
There's no doubt that when
it comes to the psychedelics

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:52.900
that are currently at the
forefront of research,

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:55.580
that ibogaine is amongst
the most riskiest ones,

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:58.520
but what's also happened
over the last three years

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:00.610
is there has been a phenomenal
amount of research done

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:02.350
with new chemical entities

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:06.100
that have de-risked it drastically.

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:09.090
So if it's something that's
de-risked in a very big way,

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:12.970
and yet is incredibly efficacious
to fight these cravings

00:11:13.925 --> 00:11:16.625
and addictive qualities that
a lot are suffering from,

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:20.130
I mean, that's immense progress

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.350
and that is something that
we're going to bet on.

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:24.700
So how do you get this
substance de-scheduled

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:27.700
and scaled out to treat the epidemic?

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:30.740
If we can actually show the efficacy rates

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:34.683
with very low toxicity
and very little harm,

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:39.320
it will naturally get through
the required clinical stages.

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.670
And once it gets through
those clinical stages,

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:44.450
there's no doubt in our minds.

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:45.860
At least I strongly believe

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:47.740
that the DEA will ultimately have

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:50.153
to take it off the Schedule I abuse list.

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:56.570
Are you at all concerned about losing

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:59.640
the Bwiti's original
shamanistic intent of this plant

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:02.620
with that sort of modern medical approach?

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:04.230
You know, we have a lot to be thankful for

00:12:04.230 --> 00:12:06.890
to a lot of the indigenous
communities around the world

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.700
that have shown us these medicines, right,

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:12.440
ibogaine in particular, but you know,

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:16.120
what was revered once as
something that was truly magical

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.770
is yet coming to the forefront, you know,

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:21.540
with all the research that's
going on, and you know,

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:23.277
as Arthur C. Clarke himself put it,

00:12:23.277 --> 00:12:26.157
"Magic is just science that
we don't understand yet."

